In commit "kernel: add KernelLogger" (95e63e954af32b2c4c7fa11a291e642ae961839d)

Minor: `Log()` takes `m_mutex` before checking `m_callbacks.empty()`, so when no logging connection is registered, every Info-and-above entry in every kernel thread still serializes on the mutex, and at debug level statements are formatted only to be dropped. The earlier `util::log::Dispatcher` avoided this with an atomic `m_callback_count`. An atomic count updated in `RegisterCallback`/`UnregisterCallback` and checked in `ShouldLog()` would cover both cases:

```c++
    bool ShouldLog(util::log::Level level) const
    {
        return m_callback_count.load(std::memory_order_relaxed) > 0 &&
               level >= m_min_level.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
    }
```

